# ForgeOps repository ignores — design.md §0.3, §14.1.
#
# Ignore generated output, the local `.env` override, tool caches and IDE state.
# NEVER ignore: licence/notice files, committed lockfiles, `.env.example`, or the
# four authoritative root documents
# (AI-Powered-DevOps-Platform-Complete-Technical-Research.md, PRD.md,
# Tech-Stack-Analysis.md, phases.md). Those are tracked inputs.
# scripts/check-hygiene.sh asserts both halves of that rule.

# ─── Local environment override (design §13.1, §13.3) ────────────────────────
# `.env` is created locally by scripts/init-env.sh; `.env.example` is committed.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# ─── Python / backend build + cache output ───────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
# Hash-pinned locks are committed (design §16.2) — never ignored.
!backend/requirements.lock
!backend/requirements-dev.lock

# ─── Go / agent build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
agent/bin/
agent/dist/
*.exe
*.test
*.prof
# `go.sum` is committed (design §16.1) — never ignored.
!agent/go.sum
# pgregory.net/rapid writes a reproduction failfile under testdata/rapid/ whenever a
# property fails. It is a debugging artifact keyed to one seed and machine, not source,
# and it appears every time a Go negative control is exercised — which would break the
# mutation harness's "working tree is clean afterwards" guarantee (design §0.4.5) for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the mutation.
**/testdata/rapid/

# ─── Node / frontend build output and caches ─────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
.pnpm-store/
*.tsbuildinfo
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
# `pnpm-lock.yaml` is committed (design §16.3) — never ignored.
!frontend/pnpm-lock.yaml

# ─── OpenTofu working state (design §10.6, §16.4) ────────────────────────────
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tofuplan.bin
crash.log
crash.*.log
# Provider lock files are committed with six-platform checksums — never ignored.
!**/.terraform.lock.hcl

# ─── Release / supply-chain output (design §8.1–§8.2) ────────────────────────
dist/
sbom/

# ─── IDE and editor state ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ─── OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ─── Local logs and scratch space ────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
tmp/
.cache/
# One-shot local scratch: `*.tmp` intermediates and `scripts/_*.py` helpers that
# generate a committed artifact once and are not part of the build. A script that
# CI or a Make target invokes never carries the `_` prefix. `scripts/_*.txt` holds
# long commit messages passed to `git commit -F`, which must not themselves become
# untracked files — the mutation harness (§0.4.5) requires `git status --porcelain`
# to be empty after a run, so scratch that is not ignored would fail it.
*.tmp
scripts/_*.py
scripts/_*.sh
scripts/_*.txt
# Captured command output kept while working a task (check exit codes, test tails,
# coverage numbers). Evidence belongs in PROGRESS.md, not in loose files, so this
# directory is deliberately never committed.
/.evidence/
# The comprehension artifact's own scratch. `docs/understand-anything/build-graph.mjs`
# and `.ua/.understandignore` are source and ARE committed; `.ua/intermediate/` holds a
# raw scan of the tree that the generator rebuilds on every run. Committing it would put
# a second, staler copy of the repository's shape under version control, and it would
# make `git status --porcelain` dirty after every regeneration — which the mutation
# harness (§0.4.5) treats as a failure.
docs/understand-anything/.ua/intermediate/
